    doc = prefix.document_ids[-1]
    token = prefix.token_ids[-1]
    if carry is not None and carry[0] == doc:
        if carry[1] == token:
            return carry, carry[2]
        return (doc, None, 0.0), 0.0
    value = initial_pulse(prefix.token_strings[-1])
    return (doc, token, value), value

"""Contextual peaks at the second digit of initial 19/20, and at English 'to'.

Number-prefix amplitudes depend on preceding words, punctuation and script;
month names and other date-like cues generally strengthen them.  The pairs
below give levels for 20 and 19 respectively.  For 'to', capitalization,
clause boundaries and the preceding word or construction set the response.
Other tokens are zero, except 0 after a noninitial 2 is weakly negative.
A short trailing text is retained, reset at each document boundary.
